{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgan3HMmKc4WdBCG5RoL4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the proof, but I couldn't check it. `lean Main.lean` fails because none of the installed Lean toolchains (v4.32.2, v4.33.0-rc1, v4.33.1, v4.35.0) contain `Init.olean`, so the standard library is missing from all of them. The error is `object file ... Init.olean of module Init does not exist`. The toolchains look incomplete or corrupted, and I haven't changed them.\n\nThis is the proof now in `Main.lean`:\n\n```lean\ninduction xs generalizing ys with\n| nil => simp [interleave]\n| cons x xs ih =>\n  rw [interleave]\n  simp [ih]\n  omega\n```\n\nThe idea is to induct on `xs` while generalizing `ys`. The `nil` case is immediate from the definition. In the `cons` case, unfolding gives `x :: interleave ys xs`, and the induction hypothesis `ih` (applied with `ys` and `xs` swapped) rewrites its length. `omega` then closes the arithmetic.\n\nIf `simp [ih]` already finishes the goal, `omega` will report \"no goals\". In that case, delete the `omega` line.\n\nReinstalling a toolchain with `elan toolchain uninstall` and then `elan toolchain install` should fix the missing files. I can do that and re-run the check if you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":246,"cache_read_input_tokens":9187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":246},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be8908c0-eee6-447a-a9b7-61dd9c363a33","uuid":"ddf48ea6-69bb-4f3f-a8ce-b97dbe08a081","timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:20:11.168Z","request_id":"req_011Cgan3H8cpEViTRmvCHHsV"}
